    "analysis_type": "flat_lexicon",
    "rationale": "No defensible multi-entry compositional paradigm survives the evidence tests. Many surface resemblances in the candidate list are accidental English orthographic overlaps (e.g. -er, -ble, wh-, bl-) without a stable shared meaning contribution across a substitution frame. The most tempting cases also fail exact compositional predictability: for example bright cannot be securely analyzed from br plus a recurring light morpheme without inventing an unsupported remainder, and syndrome-like forms such as stall, bleed, blaze, pulse, etc. bundle multiple symptoms idiosyncratically rather than combining reusable parts whose meanings add up. Standalone key-like items such as face labels (T, Bot, Fr, Bk, Lf, Rt), tool labels (B, S, F, C, Bd, L), and report markers (k, x, ?, +TAG) do not by themselves establish any attested multi-morpheme construction in this dataset. Because false morphology is worse than a flat lexicon here, all symbols are treated as opaque lexical items.",
